WEBVTT

00:00:00.338 --> 00:00:03.790
Certify Management Hub gives you one place to automate,

00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:07.869
deploy and monitor your certificates, across all of your servers.

00:00:08.733 --> 00:00:13.415
The summary shows certificate health at a glance: what's healthy, what needs attention,

00:00:13.415 --> 00:00:14.706
and what's due to renew.

00:00:15.975 --> 00:00:17.921
Adding a certificate is quick.

00:00:17.921 --> 00:00:23.759
Pick one of your IIS sites, and its domains are filled in straight from the site bindings.

00:00:23.759 --> 00:00:28.818
Every renewal is then applied back to IIS automatically, with no manual steps.

00:00:32.927 --> 00:00:34.768
Deployment tasks go further.

00:00:34.768 --> 00:00:39.502
After each renewal, the hub can export to a file share, update Exchange,

00:00:39.502 --> 00:00:43.447
Azure Key Vault or a load balancer, or run your own scripts,

00:00:43.447 --> 00:00:45.748
with dozens of task types built in.

00:00:51.519 --> 00:00:53.606
And with certificate subscriptions,

00:00:53.606 --> 00:00:57.123
a server can subscribe to a certificate managed by the hub.

00:00:57.123 --> 00:01:00.223
It's renewed once, then shared wherever it's needed.

00:01:01.074 --> 00:01:02.876
Certify Management Hub.

00:01:02.876 --> 00:01:04.443
Get started at docs.

00:01:04.443 --> 00:01:05.540
certifytheweb.

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:05.853
com.
